{"id":"chatcmpl-732da551-e64e-465c-9e7e-d2ce20fb0f6f","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246507,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a diagnostic reasoning pattern where initial assumptions about image orientation (frontal vs. lateral) were tested and revised based on expert feedback. The successful strategy involved querying a domain expert to first establish image view type, then re-querying with view-specific questions when the initial classification proved incorrect. The key insight is that ambiguous or misclassified image metadata should trigger a re-assessment with corrected context rather than proceeding with the original assumption.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a domain expert's response contradicts your initial assumption about input format or orientation, re-query with the corrected context rather than forcing the original framing.\",\n    \"Establish the fundamental properties of the input (view type, orientation, modality) before asking about specific findings, since laterality and interpretation depend on these basics.\",\n    \"Use iterative expert consultation: each query should build on prior answers, refining the question as new information (e.g., lateral vs. frontal view) emerges.\",\n    \"For laterality-dependent findings, explicitly request left-vs-right specification in the query to avoid ambiguous or default interpretations.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always confirm image view/orientation first; laterality findings (left vs. right) are meaningless without knowing the projection. Re-query if the expert's answer implies a different view than assumed.\",\n    \"Expert-assisted classification tasks\": \"Treat expert responses as diagnostic signals: if the expert's framing differs from your question's premise, adapt your next query to match the expert's framing rather than repeating the original assumption.\",\n    \"Ambiguous input disambiguation\": \"When initial metadata or assumptions about input format may be wrong, use a low-cost clarifying query before committing to a specific answer path.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm image view type (frontal/lateral) and orientation before interpreting laterality-dependent findings.\",\n    \"If expert feedback contradicts your assumed input format, re-query with the corrected context before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":449,"total_tokens":865,"completion_tokens":416,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":449},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":416}}}